l-immune crosstalk. It aims to provide a comprehensive framework for leveraging the gut microbiome in personalized lung cancer management.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9d858348408b4d384f36bfad\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Focuses primarily on lung cancer; while it mentions other cancers briefly, the detailed evidence is lung-specific. Causal inference is limited to observational associations and preclinical models.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Details the correlation between specific gut microbiota compositions (e.g., A. muciniphila, SCFA-producing bacteria) and improved clinical outcomes in solid tumors treated with ICIs. It also notes that antibiotic use negatively impacts ICI efficacy.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e20b73e0dbfc7da743e07d59\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Mechanisms are often derived from mouse models or inferred from human correlative data. The review acknowledges complexity and multiple interacting pathways rather than a single linear mechanism.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Elaborates on mechanisms including: 1) Metabolite-mediated regulation (SCFAs, acetate, butyrate influencing immune cell function); 2) Immune cell priming and trafficking (dendritic cells, T-cell activation, CD8+ T cell infiltration); 3) Direct translocation of bacteria to tumor sites; 4) Modulation of bile acid metabolism affecting Treg migration.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6ad4bdb640b37eff993589ce\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Description of the bidirectional network connecting intestinal microbiota with pulmonary health via immune, neural, and metabolic pathways.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5b85fd21d4830403e343f172\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Discussion of probiotics, prebiotics, FMT, and dietary interventions as adjuncts to immunotherapy.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e20f7ca707e5863923e328e0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Brief mentions of melanoma, renal, and bladder carcinomas regarding antibiotic impact on ICIs.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8a29b5a8633f2887be3f5fdf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review is a narrative synthesis, not a systematic review or meta-analysis; therefore, it does not provide pooled effect sizes or rigorous statistical aggregation of all available evidence.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::963355d7afe963db113a6718\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Many mechanistic claims are based on preclinical (mouse) models or correlative clinical studies; causal relationships in humans are not definitively proven within this text.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::744ca1daaa8346a24e399902\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The term 'solid tumours' in the user's plan is broader than the paper's primary focus on lung cancer; users must extrapolate carefully when applying lung-specific findings to other solid tumors.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9f82b783e138f3f0e16d8519\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c38b942335c5be7de0f70e4c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::47320b778a94a3f6e1bba0ee\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5b9018b036f8b7172a084833\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::eab85e6bee9c4b2fed5a5534\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the impact of gut microbiota/metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction followed STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: mechanisms of ICIs, heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, microbial metabolites as mediators, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and microbiome-based interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e2c9835b96f8fc6dc09ac52b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut taxa and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, highlighting context-dependent biomarkers rather than universal signatures.\",\n          \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review does not establish causal relationships for all proposed mechanisms due to observational data dominance.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4f4f27ebf49eb4765b4072a3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Anti-CTLA-4 therapy; Melanoma patients and mouse models\",\n          \"finding\": \"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for therapeutic efficacy via Th1 responses and dendritic cell activation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a1803946bf15951d555dd21c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Metastatic melanoma patients\",\n          \"finding\": \"Responders exhibit higher alpha-diversity and enrichment of Faecalibacterium and Ruminococcaceae; however, only a fraction of human taxa successfully colonize murine models.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0698d1c77cb0d200e790e2f0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Advanced NSCLC patients\",\n          \"finding\": \"Relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila is prognostic; low abundance (<4.8%) correlates with superior overall survival compared to high abundance, challenging the binary 'good/bad' bacteria concept.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::633e7982644fd55dc1491f2b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Various ICI regimens; Preclinical and clinical cohorts\",\n          \"finding\": \"Microbial influence is context-dependent: Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes associations with irAE risk invert across cancer types (protective in melanoma but linked to severe colitis in hepatobiliary malignancies).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7401efb4116390e74b3c0d15\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Mechanistic pathways; In vivo and in vitro models\",\n          \"finding\": \"Specific microbes enhance efficacy via distinct pathways: LGG and B. fragilis activate cGAS-STING; Enterococcus expresses SagA to activate NOD2; Alistipes finegoldii uses CXCL16-CXCR6 axis. Metabolites like SCFAs and indoles protect against toxicity via AhR/PPARα/NF-κB modulation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c4c101d96abe914328c6abdc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5e3f0657dbc810fb682a25e8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"To systematically characterize the complex interplay between the gut microbiome, its metabolome, and ICI outcomes (efficacy and toxicity), addressing the clinical heterogeneity in patient responses and the lack of reproducible predictive models or intervention strategies.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f3675d08d336269e9d5f7b86\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on the interaction between the gut microbiome (specific taxa and metabolites) and the efficacy/toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs), including PD-1, PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 targets. It covers preclinical mechanistic studies and early-phase clinical trials across various solid tumors (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, gastric/colorectal cancer).\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1bc1f290c28d78622ffb8469\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and their metabolic byproducts regulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). It delineates specific microbial taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e4fe0aec77d9cea7ccfbcb3b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Associations are often based on small cohorts or preclinical models. The review explicitly notes that findings are not universally reproducible and depend heavily on study methodology and cohort characteristics.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Identifies specific microbial taxa associated with ICI response across different cancer types and ICI regimens (e.g., Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1, Akkermansia abundance levels for NSCLC). Highlights that microbial roles are context-dependent and vary by tumor type and host factors.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bee8d56ffb923bd61271c4b9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are derived from murine models or in vitro studies. Human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are often undefined. The review cautions that these mechanisms may not directly translate to clinical efficacy without further validation.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Details molecular mechanisms by which microbes and metabolites modulate immunity: cGAS-STING activation by LGG and B. fragilis; NOD2 activation by Enterococcus; AhR-mediated barrier protection and cardiotoxicity mitigation by indoles and SCFAs; PERK-GSDME pyroptosis induction by TMAO.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2653a9eca08d3e9b4aabdd40\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Overview of CTLA-4, PD-1/PD-L1, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 mechanisms, and the clinical challenge of interpatient heterogeneity and irAEs.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6f7f1819fb2b6498ee2e73b4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Discussion of FMT trials (responder-derived vs. healthy donors), probiotic encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition strategies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::246f46b2e4daa7c0826508a1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Critique of current study heterogeneity, sample processing issues, and the need for standardized multi-omics approaches.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::01a4eaf6f9130e6df88a4449\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review emphasizes that microbial biomarkers are highly context-dependent (tumor type, ICI regimen, host genetics). Do not generalize findings from one cancer type (e.g., melanoma) to others (e.g., hepatobiliary) without considering this variability.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c302f1d1ebc15fb248ecf95b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models. Clinical translation is still in early phases (Phase I/II trials). Avoid overstating the clinical applicability of specific microbial interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::297962d07c0123503e761a0c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide statistical meta-analyses or formal quality assessments. Treat the synthesized evidence as indicative rather than definitive proof of causality.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4677960f83a51b4866588b1e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap question asks for a completed large randomised phase III trial of a microbiome intervention in cancer patients receiving ICIs. This study is a narrative review and does not report any completed Phase III trials. It explicitly states that 'substantial hurdles remain' and calls for 'large-scale, multicenter, standardized, longitudinal studies,' indicating that such trials were not completed or reported at the time of writing. Therefore, the success criterion of identifying a completed large Phase III trial is not met.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"The study is a narrative review that synthesizes evidence from preclinical models and early-phase clinical trials (Phase I/II) regarding microbiome interventions in cancer patients receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It details mechanisms by which specific taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) and metabolites (SCFAs, indoles, TMAO) modulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed. It highlights significant heterogeneity in study cohorts and methodologies, preventing the establishment of reproducible predictive models or definitive clinical intervention strategies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::368f88790e7cd7be69d3482e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"auxiliary_material\": \"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\",\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n            \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n            \"limitations\": [],\n            \"material_ready\": true,\n            \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n            \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap question asks for a completed large randomised phase III trial of a microbiome intervention in cancer patients receiving ICIs. This study is a narrative review and does not report any completed Phase III trials. It explicitly states that 'substantial hurdles remain' and calls for 'large-scale, multicenter, standardized, longitudinal studies,' indicating that such trials were not completed or reported at the time of writing. Therefore, the success criterion of identifying a completed large Phase III trial is not met.\",\n            \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"status\": \"unmet\",\n            \"useful_material\": \"The study is a narrative review that synthesizes evidence from preclinical models and early-phase clinical trials (Phase I/II) regarding microbiome interventions in cancer patients receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It details mechanisms by which specific taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) and metabolites (SCFAs, indoles, TMAO) modulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed. It highlights significant heterogeneity in study cohorts and methodologies, preventing the establishment of reproducible predictive models or definitive clinical intervention strategies.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8d402e4e4dd606e12c0dadf8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-0c71639dc3330990d568\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-2c047b67f79872fa4042\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-2d4faf2da7bc361a24e6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"reason\": \"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::782ec3f7244d0ab076658c3c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science Core Collection, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the effects of gut microbiota or metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction was guided by STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: first covering ICI mechanisms, then the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, followed by specific metabolite classes, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and finally microbiome-based interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d7e9648a9d3a228b80acd4f6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut microbes and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, categorizing interventions by their molecular targets (STING, NOD2, AhR, etc.).\",\n          \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review acknowledges significant methodological heterogeneity across studies and notes that many proposed biomarkers and interventions require validation in large-scale, standardized longitudinal studies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f6e33ef85bc9029ac9138418\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Melanoma patients treated with anti-CTLA-4 (ipilimumab)\",\n          \"finding\": \"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (e.g., B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for antitumor efficacy.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::69bf00aad7ea27d8d011a5f9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"NSCLC patients treated with anti-PD-1\",\n          \"finding\": \"High relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila (Akk-high) was associated with worse overall survival compared to Akk-low groups, challenging the binary 'good vs bad' bacteria concept and highlighting cohort/cancer-type dependency.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d3b8e49c5165f6a25f200eab\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Various ICI regimens\",\n          \"finding\": \"Microbial influence is context-dependent; different ICIs rely on distinct microbial signatures (e.g., Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1 vs. Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f5a2ef1b4e9581d3a710c521\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Tryptophan metabolites (3-IAld, IPA)\",\n          \"finding\": \"3-IAld alleviates colitis and enhances efficacy via AhR/IL-22; IPA provides cardioprotection via AhR/PI3K/AKT signaling.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::361feac329a052a7d78f53b7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"SCFAs (Butyrate, Propionate, Acetate)\",\n          \"finding\": \"Butyrate protects against cardiotoxicity via PPARa-CYP4X1 and enhances antigen presentation via HDAC inhibition; Propionate/Acetate promote Treg homeostasis and memory CD8+ T-cell differentiation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::120f673d74db8c5732a0396e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"TMAO\",\n          \"finding\": \"Triggers immunogenic tumor cell death (pyroptosis) via PERK-GSDME pathway, recruiting CD8+ T cells.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1b3cf17eff823e01454721f6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Probiotics (LGG, BF839, Akk)\",\n          \"finding\": \"LGG and BF839 activate cGAS-STING axis in dendritic cells to enhance CD8+ T cell infiltration; Akk produces c-di-AMP which directly activates STING.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0b0761c9932abc9ab5a5874d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"FMT interventions\",\n          \"finding\": \"FMT from long-term responders to PD-1 therapy showed higher efficacy than healthy donors; response correlated with loss of deleterious baseline species rather than just engraftment of donor strains.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6c7424e735d637988d2eced9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The clinical utility of ICIs is limited by interpatient variability in efficacy and the occurrence of systemic toxicities (irAEs). The review aims to systematically delineate the microbiome-metabolite-immune axis to understand these variations and optimize the balance between therapeutic gain and toxicity, ultimately guiding the development of precise microbial interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b70d300ebe4f7a632702a5f0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on the gut microbiome and its metabolic byproducts as systemic regulators of immune function, specifically in the context of cancer immunotherapy using immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It covers mechanisms of ICI action (PD-1/PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, TIM-3), the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions across different cancer types and cohorts, microbial metabolites (tryptophan derivatives, SCFAs, TMAO, inosine, bile acids, polyamines) as mediators of efficacy and toxicity, and microbiome-based interventions including probiotics, FMT, postbiotics, and dietary fiber.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e3b528b07174c7f2c4e9b9b5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and microbe-derived metabolites regulate the efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs) of ICIs. It highlights specific taxa like Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, and Akkermansia muciniphila that potentiate therapeutic responses via pathways such as cGAS-STING and NOD2. The review also details how microbial metabolites protect organs like the heart and colon from inflammation while enhancing anti-tumor immunity. It evaluates emerging interventions like FMT and next-generation probiotics, noting that while preclinical and Phase I trials show feasibility, substantial hurdles remain regarding cohort heterogeneity, methodological standardization, and the need for large-scale longitudinal studies to establish reproducible predictive models.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7a16470a938828a019a65473\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Critiques the reliance on single-taxa abundance, advocates for topology-based approaches, and highlights logistical barriers like metagenomic turnaround times for precision nutrition.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bf0ea10d71d03a741315fcbb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Describes FMT from responders vs. healthy donors, encapsulation technologies for probiotics, and the double-edged nature of antibiotic preconditioning and high-fiber diets.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0cebf65ae6c2fb3a2b3291c3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Findings are based on a synthesis of various studies with differing methodologies; causal relationships are often inferred from preclinical models or observational data rather than definitive clinical trials.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Details the context-dependent nature of microbiome-ICI interactions, showing that beneficial taxa vary by cancer type and ICI regimen (e.g., Bacteroides for CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium for PD-1, variable role of Akk). It also discusses the trade-off between efficacy and toxicity, noting that some microbes protective in one context may be detrimental in another.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a2d90e74ef12c1e1106eacf6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are described from murine models or in vitro studies; human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are noted as undefined.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides specific molecular mechanisms linking microbes/metabolites to immune modulation. For example, it describes how LGG and BF839 activate the cGAS-STING pathway, how tryptophan metabolites act via AhR, and how SCFAs influence T-cell function and barrier integrity through epigenetic and receptor-mediated pathways.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::74ec76742b9f6daf3762643e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide quantitative meta-analytic results; effect sizes and statistical significance should not be inferred from this text alone.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::995110f30544c2be6aece91c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models (mice) or small clinical cohorts; extrapolation to broader human populations requires caution.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b16eb73c69f940a7edbd13bf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The role of specific microbes (e.g., Akkermansia) can be context-dependent and even contradictory across studies; avoid treating any single taxon as universally beneficial or detrimental.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8d7b3fab2b1cb1884ae2d02d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Claims about the efficacy of interventions like FMT or probiotics are primarily based on early-phase trials or preclinical data; robust clinical validation is still needed.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::de02bcabb5761d1a2aab77da\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A_variants\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"approach\": \"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the impact of gut microbiota/metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction followed STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: mechanisms of ICIs, heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, microbial metabolites as mediators, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and microbiome-based interventions.\",\n            \"contribution_and_limits\": [\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut taxa and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, highlighting context-dependent biomarkers rather than universal signatures.\",\n                \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review does not establish causal relationships for all proposed mechanisms due to observational data dominance.\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"key_findings\": [\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Anti-CTLA-4 therapy; Melanoma patients and mouse models\",\n                \"finding\": \"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for therapeutic efficacy via Th1 responses and dendritic cell activation.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Metastatic melanoma patients\",\n                \"finding\": \"Responders exhibit higher alpha-diversity and enrichment of Faecalibacterium and Ruminococcaceae; however, only a fraction of human taxa successfully colonize murine models.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Advanced NSCLC patients\",\n                \"finding\": \"Relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila is prognostic; low abundance (<4.8%) correlates with superior overall survival compared to high abundance, challenging the binary 'good/bad' bacteria concept.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Various ICI regimens; Preclinical and clinical cohorts\",\n                \"finding\": \"Microbial influence is context-dependent: Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes associations with irAE risk invert across cancer types (protective in melanoma but linked to severe colitis in hepatobiliary malignancies).\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Mechanistic pathways; In vivo and in vitro models\",\n                \"finding\": \"Specific microbes enhance efficacy via distinct pathways: LGG and B. fragilis activate cGAS-STING; Enterococcus expresses SagA to activate NOD2; Alistipes finegoldii uses CXCL16-CXCR6 axis. Metabolites like SCFAs and indoles protect against toxicity via AhR/PPARα/NF-κB modulation.\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"paper_kind\": \"review\",\n            \"problem_or_question\": \"To systematically characterize the complex interplay between the gut microbiome, its metabolome, and ICI outcomes (efficacy and toxicity), addressing the clinical heterogeneity in patient responses and the lack of reproducible predictive models or intervention strategies.\",\n            \"research_scope\": \"The review focuses on the interaction between the gut microbiome (specific taxa and metabolites) and the efficacy/toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs), including PD-1, PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 targets. It covers preclinical mechanistic studies and early-phase clinical trials across various solid tumors (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, gastric/colorectal cancer).\",\n            \"work_summary\": \"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and their metabolic byproducts regulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). It delineates specific microbial taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1431bb03ae021761d8f92368\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B_variants\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"broader_review_uses\": [\n              {\n                \"connection_to_review\": \"Sets the stage for why microbiome modulation is a critical area of research in overcoming ICI limitations.\",\n                \"material\": \"Overview of CTLA-4, PD-1/PD-L1, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 mechanisms, and the clinical challenge of interpatient heterogeneity and irAEs.\",\n                \"purpose\": \"Contextual background on ICI mechanisms and limitations\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"connection_to_review\": \"Provides evidence on the feasibility and challenges of translating microbiome science into clinical practice, highlighting the gap between preclinical success and clinical implementation.\",\n                \"material\": \"Discussion of FMT trials (responder-derived vs. healthy donors), probiotic encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition strategies.\",\n                \"purpose\": \"Evaluation of microbiome-based interventions\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"connection_to_review\": \"Offers a critical perspective on the current state of the field, suggesting areas where future research needs to improve reproducibility and causal inference.\",\n                \"material\": \"Critique of current study heterogeneity, sample processing issues, and the need for standardized multi-omics approaches.\",\n                \"purpose\": \"Methodological considerations and future directions\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"facet_contributions\": [\n              {\n                \"boundaries\": \"Associations are often based on small cohorts or preclinical models. The review explicitly notes that findings are not universally reproducible and depend heavily on study methodology and cohort characteristics.\",\n                \"contribution\": \"Identifies specific microbial taxa associated with ICI response across different cancer types and ICI regimens (e.g., Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1, Akkermansia abundance levels for NSCLC). Highlights that microbial roles are context-dependent and vary by tumor type and host factors.\",\n                \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n                \"possible_uses\": \"Can be used to support arguments about the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions and the lack of a universal 'good' microbiome signature. Provides specific examples of taxa to discuss in the context of patient stratification.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are derived from murine models or in vitro studies. Human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are often undefined. The review cautions that these mechanisms may not directly translate to clinical efficacy without further validation.\",\n                \"contribution\": \"Details molecular mechanisms by which microbes and metabolites modulate immunity: cGAS-STING activation by LGG and B. fragilis; NOD2 activation by Enterococcus; AhR-mediated barrier protection and cardiotoxicity mitigation by indoles and SCFAs; PERK-GSDME pyroptosis induction by TMAO.\",\n                \"facet_id\": \"F2\",\n                \"possible_uses\": \"Provides mechanistic depth for explaining how the gut microbiome influences ICI efficacy and toxicity. Useful for discussing specific signaling pathways (STING, NOD2, AhR, NF-κB) and their role in remodeling the tumor microenvironment and protecting distal organs.\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"scope_interpretation_cautions\": [\n              \"The review emphasizes that microbial biomarkers are highly context-dependent (tumor type, ICI regimen, host genetics). Do not generalize findings from one cancer type (e.g., melanoma) to others (e.g., hepatobiliary) without considering this variability.\",\n              \"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models. Clinical translation is still in early phases (Phase I/II trials). Avoid overstating the clinical applicability of specific microbial interventions.\",\n              \"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide statistical meta-analyses or formal quality assessments. Treat the synthesized evidence as indicative rather than definitive proof of causality.\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bd2a31924b2f1b7a5c0db505\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-724817b1ad2fa81c8182\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-ba354d40740f64366cbf\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-403bce67afb0fdb07c1f\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2088384ebad86f83dd115cc2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::182a456925359bd5e4cb6b24\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"local_passages\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"external_calls\": 0,\n          \"passages\": [\n            {\n              \"best_sentence\": \"The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed.\",\n              \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2026.1803970\",\n              \"limits\": [],\n              \"match_terms\": [\n                \"粪菌移植\",\n                \"益生菌\",\n                \"机制\",\n                \"gut microbiome modulate efficacy immune checkpoint inhibitors solid tumours\",\n                \"mechanisms mediate effect\",\n                \"ici\",\n                \"i\",\n                \"ii\",\n                \"iii\",\n                \"nsclc\",\n                \"rct\"\n              ],\n              \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:290154100\",\n              \"pool_action\": \"already_in_pool\",\n              \"reading_path\": \"\",\n              \"score\": 120.720283,\n              \"section_path\": [\n                \"Supplementary question reading\"\n              ],\n              \"segment_kind\": \"directed_content\",\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0584\",\n              \"text\": \"{\\\"auxiliary_material\\\": \\\"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": [], \\\"gap_id\\\": \\\"case_E_phase3_rct\\\", \\\"judgment_path\\\": \\\"F:\\\\\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\\\\\outputs\\\\\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\\\\\03_external_closure\\\\\\\\runs\\\\\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\\\\\source_units\\\\\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\\\", \\\"limitations\\\": [], \\\"material_ready\\\": true, \\\"material_usefulness\\\": \\\"suppor…\",\n              \"title\": \"Navigating the gut–metabolite–immune axis: enhancing efficacy and mitigating toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n              \"usable_fields\": [],\n              \"year\": \"2026\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"best_sentence\": \"The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\n              \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2026.1803970\",\n              \"limits\": [],\n              \"match_terms\": [\n                \"粪菌移植\",\n                \"益生菌\",\n                \"gut microbiome modulate efficacy immune checkpoint inhibitors solid tumours\"\n              ],\n              \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:290154100\",\n              \"pool_action\": \"already_in_pool\",\n              \"reading_path\": \"\",\n              \"score\": 17.613751,\n              \"section_path\": [\n                \"general understanding\",\n                \"work summary\"\n              ],\n              \"segment_kind\": \"card_work_summary\",\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0584\",\n              \"text\": \"taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. m, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\n              \"title\": \"Navigating the gut–metabolite–immune axis: enhancing efficacy and mitigating toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n              \"usable_fields\": [],\n              \"year\": \"2026\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"question\": \"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect? 微生物干预策略的临床转化现状 系统评估粪菌移植（FMT）、活体生物药（LBPs）、益生菌及饮食干预在实体瘤 ICI 治疗中的临床试验数据，区分初治与难治人群的疗效差异，明确证据等级（I/II 期 vs III 期），并分析供体选择、安全性及标准化挑战。 涵盖人体临床试验（I-III 期），聚焦实体瘤（黑色素瘤、NSCLC、RCC、CRC 等）。包括 FMT（供体来源、给药途径）、定义菌群（如 CBM588、MRx0518）、益生菌及饮食干预。明确排除纯临床前研究（除非用于解释机制背景）及非 ICI 背景的微生物干预。严格区分观察性关联与干预性因果证据，标注试验设计类型（单臂 vs RCT）及人群特征（初治 vs 经治）。\",\n          \"reading_mode\": \"focused_local_search\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f268dc5a31e6509082426a96\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::915832e3eeeb6c7bf46b4dc7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0c9458faeedb93aae1481ce2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究采用多步骤计算与实验结合的策略：1) 利用TCGA bulk RNA-seq数据和ImmuCellAI去卷积算法，鉴定与免疫浸润负相关或正相关的TIIMGs；2) 使用L1000高通量筛选平台，针对TIIMGs筛选739种化合物的转录组扰动效应，并通过drug-to-cell recall验证；3) 在CT26小鼠模型中进行体内给药，收集肿瘤组织进行scRNA-seq，利用NMF算法从肿瘤细胞中提取异质性程序并聚类为12个MPs；4) 开发MP评分算法（结合Cluster 1激活与Cluster 2抑制的加权）量化TME重塑程度；5) 基于MP评分优先选择候选药物（oxypurinol及其前体allopurinol），通过流式细胞术、LC-MS/MS检测肌苷水平、体外共培养及体内协同实验验证机制；6) 回顾性分析人类膀胱癌患者队列中抗痛风药与抗PD-1治疗的生存关联。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::894b59684f5f72f52dd6cd62\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"建立了首个基于单细胞分辨率的药物诱导TME重塑量化框架（resTMe），定义了12个TME元程序（MPs）和MP评分算法，为预测药物-免疫疗法协同作用提供了新工具。\",\n          \"limits\": \"核心scRNA-seq数据仅来源于小鼠模型（CT26），缺乏人源类器官或PDX模型的直接验证，限制了框架在人类复杂TME中的直接外推性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8ef0876af1bde6e00dba83aa\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"发现了别嘌醇（Allopurinol）作为抗PD-1疗法的潜在增效剂，阐明了其通过嘌呤补救途径增加肌苷分泌、增强肿瘤免疫原性和T细胞功能的分子机制。\",\n          \"limits\": \"机制验证主要在体外细胞系和小鼠模型中进行；人类临床证据仅来自小样本（n=50）、单中心的回顾性观察性研究，存在混杂因素风险，需前瞻性临床试验确认。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b30b08eb075f61505bc09741\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"证实了MDSCs的耗竭是响应性TME的关键标志物，并揭示了低剂量药物可能通过非细胞毒性机制重塑TME以促进免疫浸润。\",\n          \"limits\": \"对于其他候选药物（如epirubicin, vemurafenib）的具体分子机制阐述不如AP深入；不同药物对特定免疫亚群的影响差异较大，尚未形成统一的普适性规则。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d89ef3a629b3edc8f1d5680d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"8种癌症类型TCGA数据分析\",\n          \"finding\": \"鉴定出肿瘤细胞特异性免疫浸润调节基因（TIIMGs），其中COAD拥有最多的dpGenes（792个），KIRC最少，揭示了不同癌症间TME调控网络的异质性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f9f47d7274d6ce123558914d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"L1000平台筛选739种化合物\",\n          \"finding\": \"识别出54种在多癌种中重复出现的候选药物，主要靶向CDKs、HDAC1、PI3K等通路。低剂量处理更倾向于产生非细胞毒性的免疫调节效应，而高剂量常伴随免疫抑制。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::13b75fe0affb6edd8981d33b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"CT26小鼠模型scRNA-seq分析\",\n          \"finding\": \"药物处理导致肿瘤细胞比例下降，免疫细胞（特别是巨噬细胞、DCs）浸润增加，但MDSCs显著减少。oxypurinol表现出最强的TME重塑能力，显著降低MDSCs并增加抗原呈递相关细胞。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::59223824372c97eeae14a917\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"MP评分算法应用\",\n          \"finding\": \"定义了12个MPs，其中Cluster 2（含MPs 1,3,6,8,10,12）与抗原加工和呈递通路高度相关。oxypurinol获得最高MP评分，提示其具有最强的TME重塑潜力。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4f486a10e036032c79861cfc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Allopurinol (AP) 联合抗PD-1治疗\",\n          \"finding\": \"AP通过抑制黄嘌呤脱氢酶（XDH）增加肌苷合成并分泌至胞外，肌苷上调肿瘤细胞MHC I类和PD-L1表达，增强CD8+ T细胞介导的细胞毒性。在CT26模型中，AP联合抗PD-1实现4/6小鼠完全治愈。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c5b36a5dbcaf7631b8b07425\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"人类膀胱癌回顾性队列（n=50）\",\n          \"finding\": \"在接受抗PD-1治疗的膀胱癌患者中，同时服用抗痛风药物（如AP或febuxostat）的患者组（n=7）的总生存期（OS）显著优于未服用组（n=43）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4a9ba68194211f72c5ff2998\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::309f1460bfa5781083656af4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"如何在复杂的肿瘤微环境中系统性地识别能够增强免疫疗法疗效的药物组合？目前缺乏量化药物诱导TME重塑的系统框架，且难以预测哪些非抗癌药物可作为免疫治疗的增效剂。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::732cd6b3522e68e0af8deae5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究聚焦于实体瘤（以小鼠结肠癌CT26模型和人类膀胱癌队列为主）的肿瘤微环境（TME），探讨药物诱导的TME重塑如何影响免疫检查点抑制剂（如抗PD-1/PD-L1）的疗效。研究对象包括8种癌症类型的TCGA数据、739种免疫调节化合物、小鼠体内的单细胞转录组数据以及临床回顾性队列。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::82ddeb3927993c2d17aa2d61\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究旨在解决缺乏系统性框架来量化药物诱导的TME重塑的问题。作者首先通过TCGA数据和ImmuCellAI算法鉴定了肿瘤细胞特异性免疫浸润调节基因（TIIMGs），并利用L1000平台筛选出能显著调控这些基因的化合物。随后，在小鼠CT26肿瘤模型中，通过单细胞RNA测序（scRNA-seq）分析了多种药物处理后的TME变化，识别出12个与TME重塑相关的元程序（Meta-programs, MPs）。基于MP富集情况开发了MP评分算法，用于量化TME对药物的响应程度。该算法成功鉴定出别嘌醇（Allopurinol, AP），一种痛风药物，发现其能通过促进肌苷（inosine）的合成与分泌，上调肿瘤细胞的MHC I类和PD-L1表达，从而增强CD8+ T细胞的杀伤活性。在体内实验中，低剂量AP联合抗PD-1治疗实现了4/6的小鼠完全肿瘤清除。此外，一项包含50名膀胱癌患者的回顾性研究显示，接受抗痛风药物治疗的患者在抗PD-1治疗下的总生存期显著优于未使用者。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::29799ff01275a5961dfa4b1f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"该研究未涉及肠道菌群，因此不能直接回答菌群如何调制ICI疗效的问题，只能作为平行机制或交互作用的潜在背景。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了非微生物来源的代谢物（肌苷）增强ICI疗效的证据。研究发现别嘌醇通过增加肌苷分泌，增强CD8+ T细胞功能，这与某些肠道菌群代谢产物（如丁酸盐、次级胆汁酸）调节免疫微环境的机制形成互补或对比视角。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cc0bd417229ac67f8358b8ee\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制仅限于别嘌醇-肌苷轴，不能推广为所有ICI增效剂的通用机制。人类证据仅为相关性，因果链条在人体中尚待确证。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"详细阐述了别嘌醇增强ICI疗效的具体分子机制：抑制XDH -> 增加肌苷 -> 上调MHC I/PD-L1 -> 增强T细胞杀伤。同时指出MDSCs减少是响应性TME的标志。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ce5af135f0f54a3f33ded5af\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"基于小鼠模型数据，人类组织中MDSCs的功能异质性更大，需谨慎外推。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了MDSCs耗竭作为ICI响应生物标志物的实证支持。在scRNA-seq分析中，响应性TME显著特征为MDSCs比例降低。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::911473103290b79cdeaaf990\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"别嘌醇（痛风药）被鉴定为抗PD-1增效剂，并在回顾性临床队列中显示生存获益。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d608d3703ed2d823c7784427\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"MP评分算法和12个元程序的定义，量化了抗原呈递、盐应激反应等生物学过程在药物处理后的变化。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1c11e7ad8dda921d2c87e471\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"AP处理导致肌苷大量分泌，增强OT-I T细胞对B16-OVA肿瘤的杀伤力。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9a50fe6e4b2c8671f940ffb9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究的核心对象是小鼠模型和人类膀胱癌回顾性队列，未直接研究肠道菌群。在将其用于回答‘菌群如何调制ICI’问题时，必须明确其作为‘非菌群代谢机制’的对比或补充角色，而非直接证据。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::78212dc609fe90c3f037d637\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"人类临床数据仅为小样本回顾性观察（n=50），存在选择偏倚和混杂因素，不能作为因果关系的确凿证据，仅能作为假设生成的线索。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::125505f32ce06e79d94ca2a2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"别嘌醇的机制特异性强（肌苷轴），不能将其效果泛化为所有代谢调节药物或所有ICI增效剂的共同机制。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c058dc0771a54f0d89db5a07\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"MP评分和元程序是基于小鼠CT26模型定义的，在不同癌症类型或人源模型中的适用性需进一步验证。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::50e3812052714d3b820c4e72\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The study developed a meta-program (MP) scoring algorithm based on scRNA-seq data from mouse tumors to quantify TME remodeling, identifying myeloid-derived suppressor cell (MDSC) depletion as a hallmark of responsive TMEs. It established a resource (scIMD) and web tool (resTMe) for screening immunomodulatory drugs. The analysis covered eight cancer types for gene identification but performed in vivo validation primarily in the CT26 colon carcinoma model.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"case_C2_inosine_tme\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\level2\\\\external\\\\Nf2f13ca37a1cba78c9d1-acf4314fb7d520c6\\\\round_2\\\\supplements\\\\case_C2_inosine_tme\\\\attempt-h4sdftel\\\\source_units\\\\SU03_search_candidate_7df1939f2d\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"This material does not provide the absolute physiological concentration of inosine within the human tumor microenvironment (TME); the concentration data reported is from mouse cell culture supernatants. Furthermore, it does not report a direct statistical correlation between measured human TME inosine levels and ICI efficacy (e.g., ORR, PFS, OS). The human clinical evidence provided is an association between gout medication usage (as a proxy for inosine elevation) and survival, not a correlation based on quantified inosine metabolite levels in patient tissues or fluids. The study explicitly notes its limitation that drug scRNA-seq data were derived from mouse models.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"This study investigated the synergistic effect of allopurinol (AP) with anti-PD-1 therapy. In mouse CT26 cell cultures, LC-MS/MS analysis showed AP treatment increased extracellular inosine levels by approximately 500 to 1000-fold in supernatants, while cell lysate levels remained unchanged, indicating active export. Mechanistically, AP inhibits xanthine dehydrogenase (XDH), elevating hypoxanthine which is converted to inosine via the salvage pathway. In vivo, AP combined with anti-PD-1 achieved tumor-free outcomes in 4/6 mice. In a retrospective human cohort of 50 bladder cancer patients receiving anti-PD-1 therapy, the 7 patients concurrently taking gout medications (AP or febuxostat) showed significantly better overall survival compared to the 43 patients who did not. The authors propose that elevated inosine enhances tumor immunogenicity (upregulating MHC class I and PD-L1) and supports T-cell function.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::93b0bc69434a90089e6079fe\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"auxiliary_material\": \"The study developed a meta-program (MP) scoring algorithm based on scRNA-seq data from mouse tumors to quantify TME remodeling, identifying myeloid-derived suppressor cell (MDSC) depletion as a hallmark of responsive TMEs. It established a resource (scIMD) and web tool (resTMe) for screening immunomodulatory drugs. The analysis covered eight cancer types for gene identification but performed in vivo validation primarily in the CT26 colon carcinoma model.\",\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"gap_id\": \"case_C2_inosine_tme\",\n            \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\level2\\\\external\\\\Nf2f13ca37a1cba78c9d1-acf4314fb7d520c6\\\\round_2\\\\supplements\\\\case_C2_inosine_tme\\\\attempt-h4sdftel\\\\source_units\\\\SU03_search_candidate_7df1939f2d\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n            \"limitations\": [],\n            \"material_ready\": true,\n            \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n            \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"remaining_gap\": \"This material does not provide the absolute physiological concentration of inosine within the human tumor microenvironment (TME); the concentration data reported is from mouse cell culture supernatants. Furthermore, it does not report a direct statistical correlation between measured human TME inosine levels and ICI efficacy (e.g., ORR, PFS, OS). The human clinical evidence provided is an association between gout medication usage (as a proxy for inosine elevation) and survival, not a correlation based on quantified inosine metabolite levels in patient tissues or fluids. The study explicitly notes its limitation that drug scRNA-seq data were derived from mouse models.\",\n            \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"status\": \"unmet\",\n            \"useful_material\": \"This study investigated the synergistic effect of allopurinol (AP) with anti-PD-1 therapy. In mouse CT26 cell cultures, LC-MS/MS analysis showed AP treatment increased extracellular inosine levels by approximately 500 to 1000-fold in supernatants, while cell lysate levels remained unchanged, indicating active export. Mechanistically, AP inhibits xanthine dehydrogenase (XDH), elevating hypoxanthine which is converted to inosine via the salvage pathway. In vivo, AP combined with anti-PD-1 achieved tumor-free outcomes in 4/6 mice. In a retrospective human cohort of 50 bladder cancer patients receiving anti-PD-1 therapy, the 7 patients concurrently taking gout medications (AP or febuxostat) showed significantly better overall survival compared to the 43 patients who did not. The authors propose that elevated inosine enhances tumor immunogenicity (upregulating MHC class I and PD-L1) and supports T-cell function.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::533541e5da218bf180bf8879\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-d48cd64bd12b302ad2ba\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-95bd9a77b14edf06222c\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a7194a689f46f19f0fc9\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-5f82ba52a99d38e52a55\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-5bcddf895da96806b16c\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-c44cb221036f78d05573\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"missing\": [\n                \"jitc-14-3-g001.jpg\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-g002.jpg\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-g003.jpg\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-g004.jpg\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-g005.jpg\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-g006.jpg\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s001.docx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s002.xlsx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s003.xlsx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s004.xlsx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s005.xlsx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s006.xlsx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s007.xlsx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s008.xlsx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s009.xlsx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s010.tif\"\n              ],\n              \"reason\": \"graphic_members_unmatched\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"reason\": \"supplementary_bundle_had_no_safe_matching_images\",\n              \"status\": \"unparsed\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2bb6ad04fca560d182cec1f4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::23b203078daf59896544114b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f68ab6ce48799e6ca1058cd3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用单臂、开放标签的IIa期篮子试验设计。纳入标准包括ICI治疗后疾病进展、ECOG评分0-1及可测量病灶。供体需为ICI长期响应者（>12个月响应）。干预措施包括基线后第1周和第5周通过结肠镜进行两次FMT，随后在第14、30、78周可通过灌肠进行最多三次补充FMT。ICI治疗保持不变或重新引入。主要终点评估安全性和ORR（基于iRECIST）。次要终点包括可行性、临床获益率、无进展生存期（PFS）、总生存期（OS）、微生物定植（16S rRNA测序）、免疫反应（质谱流式细胞术分析PBMCs）及生物标志物（血清细胞因子）。统计分析采用描述性统计、Kaplan-Meier生存分析及Cox比例风险模型探索免疫特征与预后的关联，未进行多重检验校正。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::35e4bb77f5eebd2aa771b705\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"证实了在ICI耐药的晚期实体瘤患者中，使用ICI响应者供体的FMT是安全和可行的。提供了关于FMT后微生物定植动力学（短暂性）和系统性免疫景观（髓系抑制与T细胞活化）的详细生物标志物数据。\",\n          \"limits\": \"样本量小（n=12），试验因入组缓慢提前终止。单臂设计无法确立因果关系，缺乏对照组。未能实现预期的临床疗效（无ORR），限制了对其机制解释的确定性。结果可能受到快速进展性疾病背景的影响，未能在足够长的时间内观察FMT的潜在延迟效应。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::59a3a7b73308240f96ffb39c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"12名ICI耐药晚期实体瘤患者，接受来自ICI响应者的FMT联合ICI治疗\",\n          \"finding\": \"FMT安全性良好，无严重FMT相关不良事件导致停药，但50%患者出现免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），多数为轻度。客观缓解率（ORR）为0%，中位PFS为1.5个月，中位OS为10.1个月。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::da136020eae35e8a2dfc6af1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"微生物组分析\",\n          \"finding\": \"首次FMT后一周，大多数受体的微生物组向供体方向偏移（定植成功），但这种相似性在后续时间点大多下降，表明定植多为暂时性。仅1名获得临床获益的患者实现了持久的供体-受体微生物相似性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0836a8c74dab91d3a0b4f4ce\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"免疫微环境分析\",\n          \"finding\": \"基线时高度分化的T细胞环境（CD8+效应记忆T细胞和TEMRA）与改善的PFS和OS相关；而髓系偏倚环境和幼稚T细胞表型预后较差。CD14+单核细胞和血清IL-8水平随时间增加，高水平的CD14+单核细胞与较短的PFS和OS相关。这些免疫特征与预后的关联在使用ICI治疗起始日期重新计算时依然成立，提示其反映的是宿主对免疫治疗的固有反应能力，而非FMT的直接因果效应。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::aa9a46960936e1395aed9137\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bbf51165ebd9be173e979c8e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"早期研究表明FMT可能逆转ICI耐药，但其适用性在其他肿瘤类型中尚不明确，且关于患者选择、供体选择及给药方案的问题仍未解决。本研究试图回答：在ICI耐药的晚期实体瘤患者中，重复FMT是否安全可行，以及是否能通过微生物定植和免疫重塑来恢复ICI的疗效。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3fb7c28aa6d5a8423ece0135\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"针对晚期实体瘤（黑色素瘤、头颈部鳞癌、肾细胞癌、微卫星不稳定性高胰腺癌）中免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）耐药或进展的患者，评估来自ICI长期响应者的粪菌移植（FMT）联合ICI治疗的安全性和有效性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b0ae5567370b869d8e867f54\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本研究是一项单臂IIa期篮子试验（MITRIC），旨在验证通过FMT调节肠道微生物群能否克服已建立的ICI耐药性。研究纳入了12名在转移性阶段对ICI治疗进展的患者，使用ICI长期响应者作为供体，给予患者最多五次FMT（前两次通过结肠镜，后续通过灌肠），并继续原有ICI治疗。主要终点为FMT相关不良事件和客观缓解率（ORR）。结果显示FMT安全性良好，但未能观察到客观肿瘤反应（ORR为0%），仅5名患者达到疾病稳定。尽管缺乏总体疗效证据，研究发现FMT诱导了短暂的微生物定植，且外周血中的免疫细胞特征（如分化T细胞与髓系细胞的平衡）与生存期显著相关，但这些免疫特征似乎更多反映疾病本身状态而非FMT的特异性干预效果。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3fb862a9266fa81e78d243db\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅适用于ICI耐药/进展人群，不能外推至一线治疗场景。样本量极小，结果可能存在偶然性，但趋势明确。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了FMT在广泛ICI耐药实体瘤队列中的真实世界疗效数据：ORR为0%，中位PFS仅为1.5个月。这表明在非选择性、快速进展的耐药人群中，FMT联合ICI并非有效的挽救疗法。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b6331b5c08533653c791a8b8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"免疫关联分析为探索性，未校正多重检验，且缺乏对照组，无法证明FMT改变了这些免疫特征从而改善了预后。仅描述了相关性，未证明因果机制。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"揭示了FMT干预后系统性免疫景观的变化及其与预后的关联：(1) FMT诱导的微生物定植多为暂时性，仅持久定植者与临床获益相关；(2) 基线高分化T细胞表型预示更好预后，而高髓系细胞（CD14+）和高IL-8水平预示不良预后；(3) 这些免疫特征似乎反映了宿主固有的免疫反应能力，而非FMT直接重塑的结果。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::38d60665b7ae5ef0786b2453\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"研究讨论了使用ICI响应者作为供体的局限性（微生物组成差异大），以及不同研究间供体数量（单供体vs多供体）对结果的潜在影响。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fd300138b8a38b7318335545\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"比较了结肠镜给药（前两次）和灌肠给药（后续）的可行性及耐受性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d1c0f5c1558648ba8264b5ed\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究的阴性结果主要归因于患者群体的快速进展特性和小样本量，不应将其解读为FMT在所有情况下均无效，而应视为特定情境下的失败尝试。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::602293d8d060926ae50da0a3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"免疫生物标志物的发现是探索性的，且可能与ICI治疗本身的效应混淆，需谨慎解读其作为FMT特异性机制的作用。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d04d310196a133922df7cbd6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"微生物定植的暂时性并不必然意味着临床无效，因为唯一获益患者的持久定植提示了两者间的潜在联系，但这仅是个案观察。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::224d056381af07f5414ea73a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"current_question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究 (MITRIC trial)\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为12名接受过多种治疗的晚期实体瘤患者（9例黑色素瘤，1例HNSCC，1例ccRCC，1例MSI-H胰腺癌），均处于ICI治疗后的疾病进展期。供体为3名长期ICI反应者。干预措施包括结肠镜给药的初始FMT和灌肠后续FMT。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在12名ICI耐药实体瘤患者中，FMT联合ICI治疗未观察到客观缓解（ORR 0%）。尽管FMT安全且可行，但临床获益有限。机制分析显示，基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚T细胞表型与较差预后相关；治疗后CD14+单核细胞和血清IL-8水平升高，这与较短的PFS和OS相关，表明FMT未能逆转这种不利的免疫微环境，甚至可能伴随髓系驱动的免疫抑制增加。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供阴性结果的详细解释，特别是关于患者选择（快速进展、晚期）、供体匹配（多供体 vs 单供体）及免疫微环境限制（髓系主导、IL-8升高），用于平衡Ch5中的阳性结果。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"Baruch et al. (2021)\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者。所有反应者均接受来自单一供体的粪便。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在一项针对抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者的概念验证试验中，使用粪便微生物移植（FMT）实现了3/10患者的客观缓解，另有3名患者获得持久的疾病稳定。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R19\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"作为对比背景，展示阳性结果中使用的单一供体策略和特定患者群体，以突显MITRIC试验中多供体和不同患者选择带来的差异。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"Davar et al. (2021)\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在一项针对抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者的试验中，FMT使3/15患者产生反应，另有3名患者获得持久的疾病稳定。响应者在FMT/抗PD-1治疗后表现出外周血中CD56+CD8+ T细胞水平升高，且这些细胞表达更高的激活标记物；同时，响应者体内循环IL-8降低，肿瘤内产生IL-8的髓系细胞频率减少。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R18\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"作为对比背景，展示阳性结果中观察到的免疫学变化（如CD56+CD8+ T细胞增加、IL-8降低），与MITRIC试验中的阴性结果形成机制上的对比。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"Kim et al. (2024)\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为抗PD-1抑制剂耐药的不可切除或转移性实体瘤患者，主要为上消化道癌症。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在抗PD-1抑制剂耐药的不可切除或转移性实体瘤患者中，FMT改善了1/13名上消化道癌症患者的抗PD-1抑制剂疗效。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R20\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"作为对比背景，展示在其他实体瘤（上消化道癌）中FMT的潜在疗效，说明癌症类型和疾病状态对结果的影响。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"MITRIC试验的阴性结果提示，FMT在克服ICI耐药方面并非普遍有效，其效果受到患者选择、供体匹配和免疫微环境状态的严格限制。\\n\\n首先，患者选择是关键因素。与之前报告阳性结果的试验（如Baruch等和Davar等）相比，MITRIC试验中的患者大多患有扩散迅速、生长快速的疾病，这可能没有给予FMT足够的时间来发挥有意义的生物学效应。此外，MITRIC试验纳入了原发性和继发性ICI耐药患者，而之前的研究主要关注继发性耐药或特定类型的耐药，这可能导致了结果的异质性。\\n\\n其次，供体匹配和多样性可能影响疗效。MITRIC试验使用了三名不同的供体，而Baruch等人的研究中所有反应者均来自单一供体。这表明，使用多名供体可能导致供体-受体匹配次优，或者缺乏对特定获益至关重要的微生物群落。供体的微生物组成存在显著差异，且目前尚不清楚使用ICI反应者作为供体是否优于健康供体。\\n\\n最后，免疫微环境的限制是重要的机制解释。MITRIC试验发现，基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚T细胞表型与较差的预后相关。治疗后，CD14+单核细胞和血清IL-8水平升高，这与较短的PFS和OS相关。相比之下，Davar等人的研究发现响应者体内IL-8降低，且髓系细胞产生的IL-8减少。这表明，在MITRIC试验的患者群体中，FMT未能逆转由髓系驱动的免疫抑制微环境，甚至可能伴随着这种抑制的增加，从而限制了临床获益。因此，FMT可能仅在具有特定免疫特征（如高分化T细胞环境、低髓系浸润）的选定人群中有效，而可靠的生物标志物尚未建立。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"MITRIC试验样本量小，且为单臂研究，无法进行因果推断或多重检验校正，因此关于免疫微环境和生物标志物的发现应谨慎解读。\",\n            \"长期定植的效果难以评估，因为大多数患者在疾病进展后无法收集后续的粪便样本。\",\n            \"需要进一步的研究来确定FMT的最佳给药方案、供体选择标准以及能够预测获益的患者亚群。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::49d98c7f1b143d31120d9835\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"paper_title\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::74660f9101b72ae9aef33244\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"plain_text\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::474c7e797e5493a25ea68330\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"prior_question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为 ICI 治疗期间或治疗后进展的晚期实体瘤患者；供体为长期 ICI 响应者；干预措施为结肠镜和灌肠给予的重复 FMT 联合持续或重新引入的 ICI 治疗；评估标准采用 iRECIST。\",\n              \"finding\": \"MITRIC 试验为一项单臂 IIa 期篮子试验，纳入 12 名对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）耐药的晚期实体瘤患者（黑色素瘤 n=9, ccRCC n=1, HNSCC n=1, MSI-H 胰腺癌 n=1）。主要终点客观缓解率（ORR）为 0/12（0%），未观察到任何客观缓解（部分或完全缓解）。5 名患者达到最佳稳定疾病（SD），7 名患者进展（PD）。中位无进展生存期（PFS）为 1.5 个月，中位总生存期（OS）为 10.1 个月。仅 1 名黑色素瘤患者获得协议定义的临床获益（SD >6 个月），另 2 名患者出现混合反应（部分病灶消退）。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供 FMT 在 ICI 耐药/难治性实体瘤患者中的具体疗效数据（ORR, PFS, OS），并展示阴性结果的具体表现，作为该人群疗效局限性的直接证据。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"作者对 MITRIC 试验结果为阴性的解释主要集中在患者选择、疾病特征及供体匹配等方面：\\n1. **患者选择与疾病进展速度**：既往研究（如 Baruch et al., Davar et al.）中的响应往往发生较晚，且有时 preceded by pseudo-progression（假性进展）。而 MITRIC 中的大多数患者表现为弥漫性、快速生长的疾病，可能没有足够的时间让 FMT 发挥有意义的生物学效应。\\n2. **供体匹配与异质性**：虽然既往研究中所有响应者均接受单一供体的粪便，而本试验使用了三名供体，可能存在次优的供体-受体匹配或缺乏产生获益所需的特定微生物群落。此外，ICI 响应者之间的微生物组成差异很大，使用健康供体是否更优尚不清楚。\\n3. **免疫微环境限制**：基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚 T 细胞表型与较差预后相关，且 FMT 未能逆转这种不利的髓系主导免疫环境（事实上 CD14+ 单核细胞和 IL-8 随时间增加，这与较短的 PFS 和 OS 相关）。这表明 FMT 可能仅在选定的具有特定免疫特征的人群中有效。\\n4. **样本量与异质性**：小样本量是重要局限性，且不同研究在供体选择、FMT 制备、给药途径和治疗方案上的异质性也可能影响结果。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"FMT 在 ICI 耐药人群中的最佳生物标志物筛选标准尚未确立。\",\n            \"供体选择（ICI 响应者 vs 健康供体）及个体化匹配策略对疗效的具体影响仍需进一步研究。\",\n            \"FMT 是否能通过改变外周血免疫表型（如减少髓系抑制）来增强疗效，目前数据不支持其诱导了显著的全身免疫改变。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f6a147f41d39b13a9ab869ee\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为 ICI 治疗期间或治疗后进展的晚期实体瘤患者；供体为长期 ICI 响应者；干预措施为结肠镜和灌肠给予的重复 FMT 联合持续或重新引入的 ICI 治疗；评估标准采用 iRECIST。\",\n              \"finding\": \"MITRIC 试验为一项单臂 IIa 期篮子试验，纳入 12 名对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）耐药的晚期实体瘤患者（黑色素瘤 n=9, ccRCC n=1, HNSCC n=1, MSI-H 胰腺癌 n=1）。主要终点客观缓解率（ORR）为 0/12（0%），未观察到任何客观缓解（部分或完全缓解）。5 名患者达到最佳稳定疾病（SD），7 名患者进展（PD）。中位无进展生存期（PFS）为 1.5 个月，中位总生存期（OS）为 10.1 个月。仅 1 名黑色素瘤患者获得协议定义的临床获益（SD >6 个月），另 2 名患者出现混合反应（部分病灶消退）。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供 FMT 在 ICI 耐药/难治性实体瘤患者中的具体疗效数据（ORR, PFS, OS），并展示阴性结果的具体表现，作为该人群疗效局限性的直接证据。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"作者对 MITRIC 试验结果为阴性的解释主要集中在患者选择、疾病特征及供体匹配等方面：\\n1. **患者选择与疾病进展速度**：既往研究（如 Baruch et al., Davar et al.）中的响应往往发生较晚，且有时 preceded by pseudo-progression（假性进展）。而 MITRIC 中的大多数患者表现为弥漫性、快速生长的疾病，可能没有足够的时间让 FMT 发挥有意义的生物学效应。\\n2. **供体匹配与异质性**：虽然既往研究中所有响应者均接受单一供体的粪便，而本试验使用了三名供体，可能存在次优的供体-受体匹配或缺乏产生获益所需的特定微生物群落。此外，ICI 响应者之间的微生物组成差异很大，使用健康供体是否更优尚不清楚。\\n3. **免疫微环境限制**：基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚 T 细胞表型与较差预后相关，且 FMT 未能逆转这种不利的髓系主导免疫环境（事实上 CD14+ 单核细胞和 IL-8 随时间增加，这与较短的 PFS 和 OS 相关）。这表明 FMT 可能仅在选定的具有特定免疫特征的人群中有效。\\n4. **样本量与异质性**：小样本量是重要局限性，且不同研究在供体选择、FMT 制备、给药途径和治疗方案上的异质性也可能影响结果。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"FMT 在 ICI 耐药人群中的最佳生物标志物筛选标准尚未确立。\",\n            \"供体选择（ICI 响应者 vs 健康供体）及个体化匹配策略对疗效的具体影响仍需进一步研究。\",\n            \"FMT 是否能通过改变外周血免疫表型（如减少髓系抑制）来增强疗效，目前数据不支持其诱导了显著的全身免疫改变。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6597e99daf38ab354bfeeb09\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究 (MITRIC trial)\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为12名接受过多种治疗的晚期实体瘤患者（9例黑色素瘤，1例HNSCC，1例ccRCC，1例MSI-H胰腺癌），均处于ICI治疗后的疾病进展期。供体为3名长期ICI反应者。干预措施包括结肠镜给药的初始FMT和灌肠后续FMT。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在12名ICI耐药实体瘤患者中，FMT联合ICI治疗未观察到客观缓解（ORR 0%）。尽管FMT安全且可行，但临床获益有限。机制分析显示，基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚T细胞表型与较差预后相关；治疗后CD14+单核细胞和血清IL-8水平升高，这与较短的PFS和OS相关，表明FMT未能逆转这种不利的免疫微环境，甚至可能伴随髓系驱动的免疫抑制增加。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供阴性结果的详细解释，特别是关于患者选择（快速进展、晚期）、供体匹配（多供体 vs 单供体）及免疫微环境限制（髓系主导、IL-8升高），用于平衡Ch5中的阳性结果。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"Baruch et al. (2021)\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者。所有反应者均接受来自单一供体的粪便。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在一项针对抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者的概念验证试验中，使用粪便微生物移植（FMT）实现了3/10患者的客观缓解，另有3名患者获得持久的疾病稳定。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R19\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"作为对比背景，展示阳性结果中使用的单一供体策略和特定患者群体，以突显MITRIC试验中多供体和不同患者选择带来的差异。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"Davar et al. (2021)\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在一项针对抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者的试验中，FMT使3/15患者产生反应，另有3名患者获得持久的疾病稳定。响应者在FMT/抗PD-1治疗后表现出外周血中CD56+CD8+ T细胞水平升高，且这些细胞表达更高的激活标记物；同时，响应者体内循环IL-8降低，肿瘤内产生IL-8的髓系细胞频率减少。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R18\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"作为对比背景，展示阳性结果中观察到的免疫学变化（如CD56+CD8+ T细胞增加、IL-8降低），与MITRIC试验中的阴性结果形成机制上的对比。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"Kim et al. (2024)\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为抗PD-1抑制剂耐药的不可切除或转移性实体瘤患者，主要为上消化道癌症。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在抗PD-1抑制剂耐药的不可切除或转移性实体瘤患者中，FMT改善了1/13名上消化道癌症患者的抗PD-1抑制剂疗效。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R20\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"作为对比背景，展示在其他实体瘤（上消化道癌）中FMT的潜在疗效，说明癌症类型和疾病状态对结果的影响。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"MITRIC试验的阴性结果提示，FMT在克服ICI耐药方面并非普遍有效，其效果受到患者选择、供体匹配和免疫微环境状态的严格限制。\\n\\n首先，患者选择是关键因素。与之前报告阳性结果的试验（如Baruch等和Davar等）相比，MITRIC试验中的患者大多患有扩散迅速、生长快速的疾病，这可能没有给予FMT足够的时间来发挥有意义的生物学效应。此外，MITRIC试验纳入了原发性和继发性ICI耐药患者，而之前的研究主要关注继发性耐药或特定类型的耐药，这可能导致了结果的异质性。\\n\\n其次，供体匹配和多样性可能影响疗效。MITRIC试验使用了三名不同的供体，而Baruch等人的研究中所有反应者均来自单一供体。这表明，使用多名供体可能导致供体-受体匹配次优，或者缺乏对特定获益至关重要的微生物群落。供体的微生物组成存在显著差异，且目前尚不清楚使用ICI反应者作为供体是否优于健康供体。\\n\\n最后，免疫微环境的限制是重要的机制解释。MITRIC试验发现，基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚T细胞表型与较差的预后相关。治疗后，CD14+单核细胞和血清IL-8水平升高，这与较短的PFS和OS相关。相比之下，Davar等人的研究发现响应者体内IL-8降低，且髓系细胞产生的IL-8减少。这表明，在MITRIC试验的患者群体中，FMT未能逆转由髓系驱动的免疫抑制微环境，甚至可能伴随着这种抑制的增加，从而限制了临床获益。因此，FMT可能仅在具有特定免疫特征（如高分化T细胞环境、低髓系浸润）的选定人群中有效，而可靠的生物标志物尚未建立。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"MITRIC试验样本量小，且为单臂研究，无法进行因果推断或多重检验校正，因此关于免疫微环境和生物标志物的发现应谨慎解读。\",\n            \"长期定植的效果难以评估，因为大多数患者在疾病进展后无法收集后续的粪便样本。\",\n            \"需要进一步的研究来确定FMT的最佳给药方案、供体选择标准以及能够预测获益的患者亚群。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fe5e2b03a837721c9a331e97\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"questions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"gap_key\": \"MITRIC 试验阴性结果需详细提取其关于患者选择、供体匹配及免疫微环境限制的解释，以平衡 Ch5 中的阳性结果。\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Supply a concrete, attributed case for the coordinated review.\",\n          \"question\": \"MITRIC 试验阴性结果需详细提取其关于患者选择、供体匹配及免疫微环境限制的解释，以平衡 Ch5 中的阳性结果。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"required_output_ids\": [\n            \"O01\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5b8ed4ce6c977fbd7aecee5c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The study provides mechanistic insights into why efficacy may be limited in certain contexts. It found that microbiota engraftment from donors was transient in most recipients, with durable engraftment observed only in the single patient who achieved clinical benefit. Mass cytometry analysis revealed that a baseline myeloid-dominant environment (high CD14+ monocytes) and high serum IL-8 were associated with poorer outcomes, while an activated T-cell signature was favorable. These immune features appeared to reflect the host's underlying disease state rather than being directly modified by FMT to improve outcomes. Additionally, the review planning material notes that this study highlights challenges in donor selection (using ICI responders vs healthy donors) and patient heterogeneity (rapidly progressive disease vs stable disease), suggesting that FMT efficacy is highly context-dependent.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"large_scale_rct_results\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260924_microbiome\\\\run01\\\\level1\\\\supplements\\\\large_scale_rct_results\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_fc8af41423\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap question asks for confirmation of completed large-scale Phase III randomized controlled trials confirming microbiome intervention efficacy. This study is explicitly identified as a 'single-arm phase IIa' trial. It is neither Phase III nor randomized. Therefore, it does not fulfill the success criterion of providing data from a completed Phase III RCT.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"This study reports the results of the MITRIC trial (NCT05286294), a single-arm, phase IIa basket trial evaluating Fecal Microbiota Transplantation (FMT) from immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) responders in patients with advanced cancers progressing on ICIs. The trial enrolled 12 patients across melanoma, head and neck squamous cell carcinoma (HNSCC), renal cell carcinoma (RCC), and microsatellite instability-high pancreatic cancer. The co-primary endpoints were safety and objective response rate (ORR). The study found that FMT was safe and feasible but demonstrated limited clinical activity: no objective responses were observed (ORR 0%), median progression-free survival was 1.5 months, and median overall survival was 10.1 months. Clinical benefit (stable disease >6 months) was achieved in only one patient. The authors conclude that FMT does not support efficacy as a salvage therapy in this non-biomarker-driven, heavily pretreated population.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::648ccd951a6ed0f6c928cb17\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"auxiliary_material\": \"The study provides mechanistic insights into why efficacy may be limited in certain contexts. It found that microbiota engraftment from donors was transient in most recipients, with durable engraftment observed only in the single patient who achieved clinical benefit. Mass cytometry analysis revealed that a baseline myeloid-dominant environment (high CD14+ monocytes) and high serum IL-8 were associated with poorer outcomes, while an activated T-cell signature was favorable. These immune features appeared to reflect the host's underlying disease state rather than being directly modified by FMT to improve outcomes. Additionally, the review planning material notes that this study highlights challenges in donor selection (using ICI responders vs healthy donors) and patient heterogeneity (rapidly progressive disease vs stable disease), suggesting that FMT efficacy is highly context-dependent.\",\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"gap_id\": \"large_scale_rct_results\",\n            \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260924_microbiome\\\\run01\\\\level1\\\\supplements\\\\large_scale_rct_results\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_fc8af41423\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n            \"limitations\": [],\n            \"material_ready\": true,\n            \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n            \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap question asks for confirmation of completed large-scale Phase III randomized controlled trials confirming microbiome intervention efficacy. This study is explicitly identified as a 'single-arm phase IIa' trial. It is neither Phase III nor randomized. Therefore, it does not fulfill the success criterion of providing data from a completed Phase III RCT.\",\n            \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"status\": \"unmet\",\n            \"useful_material\": \"This study reports the results of the MITRIC trial (NCT05286294), a single-arm, phase IIa basket trial evaluating Fecal Microbiota Transplantation (FMT) from immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) responders in patients with advanced cancers progressing on ICIs. The trial enrolled 12 patients across melanoma, head and neck squamous cell carcinoma (HNSCC), renal cell carcinoma (RCC), and microsatellite instability-high pancreatic cancer. The co-primary endpoints were safety and objective response rate (ORR). The study found that FMT was safe and feasible but demonstrated limited clinical activity: no objective responses were observed (ORR 0%), median progression-free survival was 1.5 months, and median overall survival was 10.1 months. Clinical benefit (stable disease >6 months) was achieved in only one patient. The authors conclude that FMT does not support efficacy as a salvage therapy in this non-biomarker-driven, heavily pretreated population.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::748f5657e9b651a2113dca8f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::acc00d9cd4f644b83ac0cda1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"tool_supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"allowed_use\": [],\n            \"conditions\": [],\n            \"limits\": [],\n            \"question\": \"MITRIC 试验中 FMT 在 ICI 耐药患者中的 ORR 及 PFS 数据是多少？为何结果为阴性？\",\n            \"sources\": [\n              {\n                \"doi\": \"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n                \"title\": \"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\n                \"year\": \"2026\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"still_missing\": \"MITRIC 试验中 FMT 在 ICI 耐药患者中的 ORR 及 PFS 数据是多少？为何结果为阴性？\",\n            \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供 FMT 在 ICI 耐药/难治性实体瘤患者中的具体疗效数据（ORR, PFS, OS），并展示阴性结果的具体表现，作为该人群疗效局限性的直接证据。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"MITRIC 试验为一项单臂 IIa 期篮子试验，纳入 12 名对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）耐药的晚期实体瘤患者（黑色素瘤 n=9, ccRCC n=1, HNSCC n=1, MSI-H 胰腺癌 n=1）。主要终点客观缓解率（ORR）为 0/12（0%），未观察到任何客观缓解（部分或完全缓解）。5 名患者达到最佳稳定疾病（SD），7 名患者进展（PD）。中位无进展生存期（PFS）为 1.5 个月，中位总生存期（OS）为 10.1 个月。仅 1 名黑色素瘤患者获得协议定义的临床获益（SD >6 个月），另 2 名患者出现混合反应（部分病灶消退）。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"研究对象为 ICI 治疗期间或治疗后进展的晚期实体瘤患者；供体为长期 ICI 响应者；干预措施为结肠镜和灌肠给予的重复 FMT 联合持续或重新引入的 ICI 治疗；评估标准采用 iRECIST。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"作者对 MITRIC 试验结果为阴性的解释主要集中在患者选择、疾病特征及供体匹配等方面：\\\\n1. **患者选择与疾病进展速度**：既往研究（如 Baruch et al., Davar et al.）中的响应往往发生较晚，且有时 preceded by pseudo-progression（假性进展）。而 MITRIC 中的大多数患者表现为弥漫性、快速生长的疾病，可能没有足够的时间让 FMT 发挥有意义的生物学效应。\\\\n2. **供体匹配与异质性**：虽然既往研究中所有响应者均接受单一供体的粪便，而本试验使用了三名供体，可能存在次优的供体-受体匹配或缺乏产生获益所需的特定微生物群落。此外，ICI 响应者之间的微生物组成差异很大，使用健康供体是否更优尚不清楚。\\\\n3. **免疫微环境限制**：基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚 T 细胞表型与较差预后相关，且 FMT 未能逆转这种不利的髓系主导免疫环境（事实上 CD14+ 单核细胞和 IL-8 随时间增加，这与较短的 PFS 和 OS 相关）。这表明 FMT 可能仅在选定的具有特定免疫特征的人群中有效。\\\\n4. **样本量与异质性**：小样本量是重要局限性，且不同研究在供体选择、FMT 制备、给药途径和治疗方案上的异质性也可能影响结果。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"FMT 在 ICI 耐药人群中的最佳生物标志物筛选标准尚未确立。\\\", \\\"供体选择（ICI 响应者 vs 健康供体）及个体化匹配策略对疗效的具体影响仍需进一步研究。\\\", \\\"FMT 是否能通过改变外周血免疫表型（如减少髓系抑制）来增强疗效，目前数据不支持其诱导了显著的全身免疫改变。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"allowed_use\": [],\n            \"conditions\": [],\n            \"limits\": [],\n            \"question\": \"MITRIC 试验阴性结果需详细提取其关于患者选择、供体匹配及免疫微环境限制的解释，以平衡 Ch5 中的阳性结果。\",\n            \"sources\": [\n              {\n                \"doi\": \"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n                \"title\": \"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\n                \"year\": \"2026\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"still_missing\": \"MITRIC 试验阴性结果需详细提取其关于患者选择、供体匹配及免疫微环境限制的解释，以平衡 Ch5 中的阳性结果。\",\n            \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究 (MITRIC trial)\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供阴性结果的详细解释，特别是关于患者选择（快速进展、晚期）、供体匹配（多供体 vs 单供体）及免疫微环境限制（髓系主导、IL-8升高），用于平衡Ch5中的阳性结果。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在12名ICI耐药实体瘤患者中，FMT联合ICI治疗未观察到客观缓解（ORR 0%）。尽管FMT安全且可行，但临床获益有限。机制分析显示，基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚T细胞表型与较差预后相关；治疗后CD14+单核细胞和血清IL-8水平升高，这与较短的PFS和OS相关，表明FMT未能逆转这种不利的免疫微环境，甚至可能伴随髓系驱动的免疫抑制增加。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"研究对象为12名接受过多种治疗的晚期实体瘤患者（9例黑色素瘤，1例HNSCC，1例ccRCC，1例MSI-H胰腺癌），均处于ICI治疗后的疾病进展期。供体为3名长期ICI反应者。干预措施包括结肠镜给药的初始FMT和灌肠后续FMT。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"Baruch et al. (2021)\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"作为对比背景，展示阳性结果中使用的单一供体策略和特定患者群体，以突显MITRIC试验中多供体和不同患者选择带来的差异。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在一项针对抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者的概念验证试验中，使用粪便微生物移植（FMT）实现了3/10患者的客观缓解，另有3名患者获得持久的疾病稳定。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"研究对象为抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者。所有反应者均接受来自单一供体的粪便。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": [\\\"R19\\\"]}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"Davar et al. (2021)\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"作为对比背景，展示阳性结果中观察到的免疫学变化（如CD56+CD8+ T细胞增加、IL-8降低），与MITRIC试验中的阴性结果形成机制上的对比。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在一项针对抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者的试验中，FMT使3/15患者产生反应，另有3名患者获得持久的疾病稳定。响应者在FMT/抗PD-1治疗后表现出外周血中CD56+CD8+ T细胞水平升高，且这些细胞表达更高的激活标记物；同时，响应者体内循环IL-8降低，肿瘤内产生IL-8的髓系细胞频率减少。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"研究对象为抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": [\\\"R18\\\"]}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"Kim et al. (2024)\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"作为对比背景，展示在其他实体瘤（上消化道癌）中FMT的潜在疗效，说明癌症类型和疾病状态对结果的影响。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在抗PD-1抑制剂耐药的不可切除或转移性实体瘤患者中，FMT改善了1/13名上消化道癌症患者的抗PD-1抑制剂疗效。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"研究对象为抗PD-1抑制剂耐药的不可切除或转移性实体瘤患者，主要为上消化道癌症。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": [\\\"R20\\\"]}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"MITRIC试验的阴性结果提示，FMT在克服ICI耐药方面并非普遍有效，其效果受到患者选择、供体匹配和免疫微环境状态的严格限制。\\\\n\\\\n首先，患者选择是关键因素。与之前报告阳性结果的试验（如Baruch等和Davar等）相比，MITRIC试验中的患者大多患有扩散迅速、生长快速的疾病，这可能没有给予FMT足够的时间来发挥有意义的生物学效应。此外，MITRIC试验纳入了原发性和继发性ICI耐药患者，而之前的研究主要关注继发性耐药或特定类型的耐药，这可能导致了结果的异质性。\\\\n\\\\n其次，供体匹配和多样性可能影响疗效。MITRIC试验使用了三名不同的供体，而Baruch等人的研究中所有反应者均来自单一供体。这表明，使用多名供体可能导致供体-受体匹配次优，或者缺乏对特定获益至关重要的微生物群落。供体的微生物组成存在显著差异，且目前尚不清楚使用ICI反应者作为供体是否优于健康供体。\\\\n\\\\n最后，免疫微环境的限制是重要的机制解释。MITRIC试验发现，基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚T细胞表型与较差的预后相关。治疗后，CD14+单核细胞和血清IL-8水平升高，这与较短的PFS和OS相关。相比之下，Davar等人的研究发现响应者体内IL-8降低，且髓系细胞产生的IL-8减少。这表明，在MITRIC试验的患者群体中，FMT未能逆转由髓系驱动的免疫抑制微环境，甚至可能伴随着这种抑制的增加，从而限制了临床获益。因此，FMT可能仅在具有特定免疫特征（如高分化T细胞环境、低髓系浸润）的选定人群中有效，而可靠的生物标志物尚未建立。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"MITRIC试验样本量小，且为单臂研究，无法进行因果推断或多重检验校正，因此关于免疫微环境和生物标志物的发现应谨慎解读。\\\", \\\"长期定植的效果难以评估，因为大多数患者在疾病进展后无法收集后续的粪便样本。\\\", \\\"需要进一步的研究来确定FMT的最佳给药方案、供体选择标准以及能够预测获益的患者亚群。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4d15b90b1b4387e8af2a1be3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8e24c98ddc10d25e6368e25c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c7751d6078705a8eed77bd20\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b7b7e3472b4df79f76e0d24c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用叙述性综述方法，综合了机制研究（前临床模型与人类观察数据）和临床干预试验证据。具体路线包括：1）梳理微生物组影响ICI的药理学基础（抗原呈递、代谢物耦合、屏障完整性）；2）分类评估三类主要干预手段（FMT、LBPs、定义菌群）的代表性临床试验结果；3）讨论影响可重复性的转化因素（共用药、饮食、定植率）及安全监管问题。未进行系统检索或定量荟萃分析，而是基于现有文献进行逻辑整合与批判性评议。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d823b853e4ac54a493eee6ef\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了关于微生物组工程化干预ICI治疗的最新临床证据综合，特别区分了FMT、LBPs和定义菌群三种模态的优缺点及适用场景。\",\n          \"limits\": \"作为迷你综述，未提供新的原始实验数据；对特定菌株或代谢物的因果机制多基于前临床模型或间接人类证据，缺乏大规模随机对照试验的确证数据。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cdc0eb48bfb3cc26a577a419\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提出了将微生物组干预视为“生态药理学”而非简单附加剂的框架，强调了基线生态、共用药和功能性读出（如代谢物、定植率）的重要性。\",\n          \"limits\": \"对于不同肿瘤类型间微生物组效应的异质性解释有限，主要依赖已发表的小规模试验，难以推断普适性规律。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c698a9fd6f94a8050dbc3115\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"明确了安全与监管优先事项，包括供体筛查、追溯性及报告标准，为未来临床试验设计提供了实用指南。\",\n          \"limits\": \"监管建议基于现有案例和专家共识，尚未形成统一的行业标准，具体实施细节尚待后续研究明确。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::698814d6ffd5131ce300e4d6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"抗PD-1难治性转移性黑色素瘤\",\n          \"finding\": \"来自反应者的粪菌移植（FMT）提供了最强的人类概念验证，部分患者实现了临床再敏感化，并伴随供体型微生物特征和肿瘤免疫重塑。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8fa931de280fc236eee06476\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"使用活体生物制剂（如CBM588）联合ICI\",\n          \"finding\": \"在肾细胞癌中显示出改善临床结果的探索性信号，且能显著改变粪便微生物组特征，但结果具有情境依赖性，需更多大样本验证。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4ccc398d5ad7381abec37394\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"使用定义菌群（如SER-401）及抗生素预处理\",\n          \"finding\": \"一项针对黑色素瘤的Ib期试验因入组不足未能得出效力结论，但揭示了广谱抗生素预处理可能破坏保护性免疫准备，提示“清除后添加”策略存在设计陷阱。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::46a823fe6dc2d69e904ef7b1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"ICI相关的难治性结肠炎\",\n          \"finding\": \"FMT在病例系列和转化研究中显示出修复生态平衡、恢复黏膜免疫耐受的活动，支持其作为毒性管理的潜在手段。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7235049ddd5daa54ae6a8121\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1fc6d62ba3897e0fe7ee791b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管ICIs改变了多种恶性肿瘤的管理方式，但仅对部分患者有效且伴随毒性。现有的组织生物标志物无法完全捕捉宿主层面的决定因素。本研究试图解决的核心问题是：肠道微生物组如何作为可操作的调节器影响ICI的敏感性和毒性？以及目前基于微生物组的临床干预策略（FMT、LBPs、Consortia）的证据基础和转化障碍是什么？\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0de486040443081d8ed9cbc1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"聚焦于实体瘤（特别是黑色素瘤、肾细胞癌、非小细胞肺癌等）患者接受免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs，如抗PD-1/CTLA-4治疗）时的疗效与毒性管理。研究对象为肠道微生物组及其工程化干预策略，涵盖从基础机制到临床转化试验的综合分析。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::08bc0ccb88530457d6c7da11\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本文是一篇迷你综述，旨在将微生物生态学原理与抗原呈递、T细胞启动及代谢物信号传导等生物学机制联系起来，并系统总结了三种主要干预模式（粪菌移植FMT、活体生物制剂LBPs、定义菌群Consortia）的临床证据。文章指出，肠道微生物组不仅是预测标志物，更是可操作的宿主水平调节剂，能够同时影响抗肿瘤疗效和免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）。通过回顾早期临床试验，作者强调了微生物组干预在重新敏感化难治性肿瘤中的概念验证价值，同时也指出了当前干预措施在可重复性、安全性及标准化方面的挑战。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c38bcef62c8079a6036e37c8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"证据主要来自小规模Phase 1/Ib期试验，样本量小，异质性高。不能直接外推至所有一线治疗场景或所有肿瘤类型。特别是SER-401试验未达效力终点，需谨慎解读。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了三类主要微生物组干预策略（FMT、LBPs、Consortia）在实体瘤中的具体临床证据对比。例如，FMT在难治性黑色素瘤中显示出的概念验证效力，以及LBPs在肾细胞癌中的探索性信号。同时指出了定义菌群试验中因抗生素预处理导致的负面设计教训。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0e83796c6787bdce34f2f296\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"许多机制细节源自前临床模型（小鼠），人类证据多为间接支持（如FMT后的免疫重塑观察）。代谢物水平的因果关系在人类中尚未完全确立，需注意区分观察性关联与因果证据。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"详细阐述了微生物组影响ICI疗效的生物学机制框架，包括：1）通过促进树突状细胞激活和交叉呈递来增强CD8+ T细胞反应；2）通过短链脂肪酸等代谢物调节先天免疫编程和炎症基调；3）通过维持肠道屏障完整性来减少系统性炎症和irAEs风险。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d86b2c26e65d14b0a2de91e0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"讨论了基线生态、共用药（抗生素、PPI、激素）、饮食和定植率对干预结果的影响。强调了‘生态药理学’概念，即干预不是简单的药物添加，而是生态扰动。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8449be79b3a7045e41c5dacb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"提到了耐药大肠杆菌血症、产志贺毒素大肠杆菌以及SARS-CoV-2传播的案例，强调了供体筛查和制造控制的重要性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5c4718a22ebccf62e6d86dfd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该论文主要关注实体瘤（黑色素瘤、肾细胞癌、NSCLC），其结论不一定适用于血液肿瘤或其他癌症类型。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::434f935a5128024bbc9228db\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"文中提到的‘强概念验证’仅限于抗PD-1难治性黑色素瘤中的FMT，不应过度推广到其他干预模式或肿瘤类型。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::736f594938f6aedd75c4d1dd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"机制部分混合了前临床模型和人类观察数据，需明确区分哪些是已证实的人类因果机制，哪些是基于模型的推测。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b0fe5dc8f31ddf0d2f44a79a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"临床试验结果多为早期阶段（Phase 1/Ib），效力结论往往受限（如SER-401试验），解读时需强调其探索性质。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e325d70a97f845ed6b9630a4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0be30e1c595392c045092cd7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f738899367563eaec3b1317e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5385a7857d92f184b107095e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"遵循PRISMA指南进行系统综述。使用Covidence管理流程，检索特定关键词组合。纳入标准为成人实体瘤患者，排除非英语、非人类、评论类文章。数据提取包括患者数量、ICI类型、癌症类型、干预措施及其对微生物多样性、OS、PFS和irAE的影响。未进行荟萃分析（因已有相关Meta分析且异质性高），而是采用定性综合方法，对比抗生素组与非抗生素组、FMT干预前后的临床结局和免疫学指标。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8a995b8b38ea63be01d384b5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了截至2021年的系统性证据汇总，确认抗生素使用与ICI疗效降低的强关联，以及FMT在逆转耐药和管理irAE方面的潜在益处。\",\n          \"limits\": \"1. 未进行定量Meta分析，限制了效应量的精确估计。2. 纳入研究多为观察性或小样本临床试验，存在选择偏倚和混杂因素（如合并用药、饮食、种族信息缺失）。3. OS和PFS定义不统一，影响结果可比性。4. FMT研究样本量极小，且部分患者在使用FMT前接受了强效免疫抑制剂，干扰因果推断。5. 缺乏关于抗生素种类、剂量及具体微生物群落变化的详细数据。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f61397f7ac6f10ccd811c334\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"抗生素使用（主要覆盖NSCLC, RCC, Melanoma，靶向PD-1/PD-L1为主），时间窗多为ICI开始前2个月至开始后1个月内\",\n          \"finding\": \"21/22项研究显示抗生素对OS和/或PFS有显著的负面影响。例如，Schett et al. (2019)中NSCLC患者抗生素组OS为1.8 vs 15.4个月；Pinato et al. (2019)中pATB组OS为2 vs 26个月。部分研究（如Lalani et al., Balado et al.）未发现显著差异，但总体趋势为负面。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::62930893a334abdd4a90dacc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"FMT用于ICI耐药或发生严重irAE的实体瘤患者（主要为黑色素瘤，少量前列腺癌/尿路上皮癌）\",\n          \"finding\": \"所有6项FMT研究显示积极效果。Davar et al. (2019)中40%耐药患者克服耐药；Youngster et al. 和 Baruch et al. 分别报告60%和30%的患者克服耐药，伴随CD8+ T细胞浸润增加和IL-8下调。Wang et al. (2018, 2020)显示FMT可缓解ICI诱导的结肠炎（73%临床响应）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::75ab64b8a6712b9b3a7d5e44\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e70d3f39722026e27b2d7bed\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"1. 肠道微生物群改变药物（主要是抗生素）是否会对ICI的疗效产生不利影响？2. FMT是否能通过恢复肠道微生物群来改善ICI疗效并降低irAE的发生率？\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ec580adacab9bbedb26ba339\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"针对晚期实体瘤患者，考察肠道微生物群改变药物（主要为抗生素及其他伴随用药）和粪便微生物群移植（FMT）对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效（总生存期OS、无进展生存期PFS）及毒性（免疫相关不良事件irAEs）的影响。纳入2015年1月至2021年4月发表的英文研究。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e6de935b19653fcb6e426043\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"这是一篇系统综述，旨在评估肠道菌群调节干预措施与ICI治疗结果之间的关联。作者检索了OVID Medline、Embase等数据库，筛选出28项符合标准的研究：其中22项关注抗生素/其他药物对ICI疗效的影响，6项关注FMT对ICI疗效及irAE减轻的作用。结果显示，绝大多数（21/22）涉及抗生素的研究表明其显著降低OS和/或PFS；所有6项涉及FMT的研究均显示其在恢复ICI疗效或减少irAE方面具有积极效果。综述同时指出了现有研究在定义终点、样本量、混杂因素控制等方面的局限性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::91e994144d313746f98c75e2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅基于回顾性队列和小样本前瞻性研究，无法确立严格的因果关系；不同癌症类型和ICI亚型的效果可能存在差异（尽管多数为PD-1/PD-L1抑制剂）。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了抗生素使用导致ICI疗效下降的大规模临床观察证据（21/22研究支持），以及FMT改善疗效的具体案例数据。明确了肠道菌群状态是ICI疗效的重要预测/影响因素。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3f83ec56f5f6859978c91322\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制描述主要来自少数几个高质量的小样本研究（如Davar, Youngster, Baruch），其他研究多仅报告临床结局；部分机制（如IL-8下调）尚未在所有FMT研究中得到一致验证；需区分是直接由菌群引起还是继发于免疫状态改变。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"揭示了FMT起效的部分潜在免疫机制：增加CD8+ T细胞浸润、增加抗原呈递细胞（CD68+）、下调促耐药因子IL-8及其产生的髓系细胞。这些发现直接指向了T细胞介导的抗肿瘤免疫增强和炎症微环境改善。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::721f781a7291a3c4ccd59163\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"综述指出大多数纳入研究集中在NSCLC, RCC, Melanoma，且主要使用抗PD-1/PD-L1药物。同时提到化疗等其他抗癌治疗也可能破坏肠道屏障和菌群。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e16271ee6436c84aa68cc464\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"综述详细分析了纳入研究在OS/PFS定义上的不一致性，以及FMT研究中随机化困难、样本量小、合并用药（免疫抑制剂）带来的偏倚风险。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7c5de44e3cb32833abfeb875\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"建议未来研究应关注抗生素使用时机（提前vs同期）、具体抗生素种类/剂量、患者种族/饮食对菌群的影响，以及扩大FMT研究的样本量。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6daa6bf638fc0a586c155313\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"FMT的积极结果主要来源于小样本、单臂或开放标签研究，且部分患者在使用FMT前已接受过强效免疫抑制治疗，因此不能简单外推为FMT对所有ICI耐药患者的普适性解决方案。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::03d903e6472f77e8ddd42f80\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"抗生素的负面影响虽在多数研究中观察到，但存在例外（如Lalani, Balado等），这可能源于抗生素类型、给药时机或癌症类型的差异，需谨慎归因。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::75b33df0d637c35db8e354cf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"综述未进行Meta分析，因此提供的效应方向是定性的，缺乏统一的效应量估计。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1b51b4a793d85bd67eec15e5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"机制性发现（如IL-8, CD8+ T cells）主要来自少数几项深入生物学分析的研究，不代表所有临床观察到的疗效变化都有相同的机制基础。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1300bff91406c33fa664d068\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-724817b1ad2fa81c8182\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::07d9c6e4c1bb2933d52092e4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::84b32c303722590ec2d53121\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6befe43108931f970e929b2e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"As a review article, this work does not present new primary experimental data but synthesizes existing literature. The authors systematically summarize findings from retrospective clinical studies, prospective cohorts, and preclinical murine models regarding the correlation between gut microbiota composition (diversity, specific taxa like Faecalibacterium, Bifidobacterium, Bacteroides) and ICPI outcomes. They integrate mechanistic insights from immunology (T-cell regulation, dendritic cell maturation) and metabolism (short-chain fatty acids, bile acids). The approach involves categorizing evidence into themes: response prediction, toxicity mediation (colitis, myocarditis), antibiotic effects, and therapeutic manipulation (FMT, probiotics, synthetic biotics), supported by tables listing relevant clinical trials.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c5f0af15908b0603befc98d6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive synthesis of the dual role of the gut microbiome in determining both the efficacy and toxicity of ICPIs in solid tumors. It integrates clinical associations with mechanistic hypotheses (immunological and metabolic) and maps the landscape of ongoing clinical trials for microbiome-based therapies.\",\n          \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it does not perform a systematic meta-analysis or provide quantitative pooled estimates. The mechanistic explanations are largely derived from preclinical models or correlative human studies, so causal relationships remain to be fully validated in large-scale randomized controlled trials. The review acknowledges heterogeneity in findings across different cancer types and geographic populations.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::01f63df59d963a0044ad8942\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Solid tumor patients receiving ICPIs (anti-PD-1/PD-L1, anti-CTLA-4)\",\n          \"finding\": \"Loss of microbial diversity (dysbiosis) and enrichment of certain bacteria (e.g., Faecalibacterium, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) are associated with improved objective response rates and survival, while depletion of these taxa or enrichment of others (e.g., Bacteroides) correlates with poor response.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d4337ee1dd2b52b96d4bd29a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Patients treated with broad-spectrum antibiotics prior to or during ICPI therapy\",\n          \"finding\": \"Antibiotic use is consistently associated with reduced overall survival and progression-free survival, likely due to disruption of beneficial gut microbiota; narrow-spectrum antibiotics show less clear detrimental effects.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0cdc25ae78468f915b4f1e1c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Development of immune-related adverse events (irAEs), particularly colitis and myocarditis\",\n          \"finding\": \"Specific bacterial strains influence irAE risk; e.g., Faecalibacterium enrichment is linked to higher incidence of colitis but better tumor response, while Bacteroidetes may protect against colitis. Mechanisms involve cross-reactive T-cells primed by bacterial peptides (e.g., beta-galactosidase from Bacteroides) targeting host tissues (e.g., MYH6 in heart).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b8a5d96c854e7ba7964eeaa9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Preclinical and early-phase clinical trials of microbiome modulation\",\n          \"finding\": \"Interventions such as FMT, oral live biotherapeutics (e.g., EDP1503, SER-401), and synthetic biotics are being tested to restore microbiome diversity or introduce beneficial strains, showing preliminary promise in enhancing ICPI efficacy or managing refractory colitis.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::05e383c2aae7e03a620e4828\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bb6006227f00f1e06386e3bd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review addresses the challenge that only a minority of cancer patients derive durable benefit from ICPIs, and many experience severe irAEs. It seeks to explain why responses vary among patients by examining the gut microbiome as a potential predictive biomarker and modulator of both therapeutic efficacy and toxicity, aiming to identify avenues for improving patient outcomes through microbiome-targeted strategies.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::00719742511ab12e73100aea\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on the role of the gut microbiome in modulating response and toxicity to immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICPIs) in cancer patients, with specific emphasis on solid tumors (e.g., melanoma, non-small cell lung cancer, renal cell carcinoma, pancreatic adenocarcinoma). It covers clinical observations, preclinical mechanisms, and emerging therapeutic strategies involving microbiome modulation.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f6b85ed0929d25a175964026\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This article is a narrative review summarizing current evidence on how the gut microbiome influences the efficacy and safety of ICPI therapy. It discusses the association between microbial diversity/composition and treatment outcomes, outlines putative immunological and metabolic mechanisms linking gut bacteria to anti-tumor immunity and immune-related adverse events (irAEs), and highlights the impact of antibiotics and dietary factors. The review also surveys ongoing clinical trials evaluating microbiome-based interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) and live biotherapeutics to enhance ICPI response or mitigate toxicity.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d93757978c699f59d944785e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Associations are primarily observational or from small prospective studies; causality is not established. Findings may vary by cancer type and geography. Does not provide definitive proof of mechanism.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Summarizes clinical evidence linking specific gut microbial signatures (e.g., Faecalibacterium, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium vs. Bacteroides) to ICPI response rates and survival outcomes in solid tumors. Details the negative impact of broad-spectrum antibiotic use on treatment efficacy.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ef1a42d6b6dd05fa51875187\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are derived from murine models or correlative human data. The exact pathways are described as 'putative' and 'not fully elucidated'. Direct causal links in humans require further validation. Specific peptide-crossreactivity details are based on specific transgenic models.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Details putative mechanisms including: 1) Modulation of T-regulatory cells and antigen-specific T-cell accumulation in the tumor microenvironment; 2) Production of metabolites (SCFAs, deoxycholate) influencing anti-tumor tolerogenesis; 3) Cross-reactive T-cell activation via bacterial peptides (e.g., beta-galactosidase mimicking MYH6) leading to irAEs like myocarditis; 4) Role of intraepithelial lymphocytes and dendritic cells in colitis pathogenesis.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d93afb5e20374119e59c09bb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Introduction section discussing the paradigm shift in cancer treatment, the lack of universal predictive biomarkers, and the growing interest in the tumor microenvironment and gut microbiome.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1c51da46bff8a9c0bbd953a0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Table 1 and Table 2 listing phase I/II trials evaluating microbial therapies (EDP1503, SER-401, MRx0518, FMT) in various solid tumors and for managing irAEs.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a9c949dec2c60440905ab78b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Section on 'Antibiotic mediated modulation...' and mentions of dysbiosis causes in the toxicity section.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e88468e5ba9034039695a162\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review is a narrative synthesis, not a systematic review with strict inclusion/exclusion criteria or meta-analytic statistics. Claims should be interpreted as summaries of emerging trends rather than definitive consensus.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b93a566b8c782cd7c5da194b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Mechanistic insights are largely based on preclinical models (mice) or correlative human studies; causal inference in humans is limited.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::79c03182deb792dead1afbfa\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Findings on specific bacterial taxa may vary across different cancer types, geographic regions, and study populations. Generalizations should be made cautiously.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a3ec7b906bce3050cdf0fb32\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The term 'solid tumors' is used broadly; specific results may apply only to certain cancers (e.g., melanoma, NSCLC, RCC).\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9a60373c4ec7d897e091ba05\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"fiel